[FEN "r7/2pk2p1/2b1p3/4PP1p/7P/3BK1P1/8/2R5 b - - 0 34"]
[SetUp "1"]
[Site "https://lichess.org/analysis/r7/2pk2p1/2b1p3/4PP1p/7P/3BK1P1/8/2R5_b_-_-_0_34"]

{ At first glance this looks like a dead drawn ending, both sides down to just a rook, a bishop and a handful of pawns apiece. } 34... Ra3 { His rook swings out to grab the third row, but that busy-looking move ignores something far more urgent — his king is still just one square from real trouble. } 35. fxe6+ { Your pawn captures with check and drags his king onto e six whether he likes it or not — now look down the open c column at what waits there. [%csl Rc6] } (35. Kf4 { Stepping the king to safety on f four looks perfectly sensible, but it leaves the position completely, dead level. } 35... Bd5 36. Be2 exf5 37. Bxh5 c6 { The king tucks itself away and the pawns trade off, and nothing about the position has changed at all. }) (35. Ke2 { Stepping the king out of the pin on e two feels careful, but the moment to drag him onto e six is gone for good. } 35... Bf3+ 36. Kd2 Bd5 37. f6 gxf6 { The king slips out through e two untouched, and the position settles right back to equal. }) 35... Kxe6 { He has no real choice but to recapture with the king. Now look closely at what his king on e six and his bishop on c six have in common. [%csl Re6] } 36. Rxc6+ { Your rook scoops up the bishop with check, and the pawn sacrifice two moves ago did every bit of the work — that is the decoy paying off. } (36. Kf4 { Chasing the rook with your own king forgets the much bigger prize: the check on c six that wins the bishop outright. } 36... Ra4+ 37. Rc4 Rxc4+ 38. Bxc4+ Ke7 { After all that manoeuvring you only reach a drawn rook ending, when the bishop was there for the taking. }) (36. Kd4 { Marching the king forward looks active enough, but it leaves a free bishop sitting on the board completely untouched. } 36... Bd5 37. Rxc7 Ra4+ 38. Ke3 Ra3 { You grab a pawn back, but giving his bishop time to plant itself on d five lets him hold the balance. }) 1-0


[Event "Intermediate tactics: decoy with a bishop"]
[Result "1-0"]
[Role "exercise"]
