[FEN "1r4k1/p1p2ppp/2P1p3/3pP3/1B3P1b/P3q2P/2Q3P1/5R1K b - - 1 24"]
[SetUp "1"]
[Site "https://lichess.org/analysis/1r4k1/p1p2ppp/2P1p3/3pP3/1B3P1b/P3q2P/2Q3P1/5R1K_b_-_-_1_24"]

{ Now for interference: put one of your own pieces right on the defender's line, and it suddenly goes blind to everything it was guarding behind it. } 24... Bg3 { His bishop leaps all the way to g three, deep inside your position — but slide your rook to f three, and you cut the very line his queen uses to watch it. [%cal Yf1f3][%csl Rg3] } 25. Rf3 { His queen was guarding that bishop all the way along the third row, and your rook now sits squarely in between them, blocking her view of it completely. [%cal Re3g3] } (25. Bc5 { Attacking the queen head on with the bishop looks direct enough, but she simply offers a trade and the position settles down. } 25... Qb3 26. Qxb3 Rxb3 27. Rf3 Rb1+ { Queens and rooks come off the board, and you are left with a plain equal ending instead of the whole bishop. }) (25. Bd6 { The bishop finds a pretty-looking square on d six, but there is nothing behind it — his queen still watches g three just fine. } 25... Qb6 26. Qc3 Qb5 27. Ra1 Bxf4 { He is completely fine, and along the way you have simply dropped a pawn of your own for no reason. }) 25... Qd4 { His queen has to step off the third row to escape your rook, and once she moves she can no longer see the bishop sitting on g three at all. [%csl Rg3] } 26. Rxg3 { A whole bishop. Your rook cut the queen's line, and the bishop she was defending is yours for nothing. That is interference. } (26. Qc1 { Defending your own back row with the queen forgets all about the bishop that is still hanging on g three. } 26... Bh4 27. Kh2 h5 28. Qg1 Qxg1+ { His bishop calmly steps away to h four, and the piece you were about to win has simply got away. }) (26. Qc5 { Offering a queen trade here ignores a free piece sitting right there on the board, waiting to be collected instead. } 26... Qxc5 27. Bxc5 Rb1+ 28. Bg1 Bh4 { You traded queens instead of collecting the loose bishop on g three — it is still sitting there for him. }) 1-0


[Event "Intermediate tactics: interference on the diagonal"]
