[FEN "3r1rk1/p2nppbp/2p2np1/qpPp4/N2P1B2/PP1BP2P/5PP1/R2Q1RK1 b - - 0 15"]
[SetUp "1"]
[Site "https://lichess.org/analysis/3r1rk1/p2nppbp/2p2np1/qpPp4/N2P1B2/PP1BP2P/5PP1/R2Q1RK1_b_-_-_0_15"]

{ A queen has wandered a long way from home in search of material, and her path back is about to narrow very fast indeed. } 15... bxa4 { His pawn grabs your knight on a four, but his queen is still stranded far from safety on the other side of the board. } 16. b4 { Your pawn steps forward and takes another one of her escape squares away — after this move, she has exactly one square left to run to. [%csl Ra5] } (16. Rb1 { Defending the pawn quietly with the rook gives her queen exactly the time she needs to escape, knight and all. } 16... axb3 17. Rxb3 e5 18. Bh2 Ne4 { You are left a whole piece down for nothing, and the queen has long since made her way back to safety. }) (16. Bg3 { A quiet developing move for the bishop ignores the fact that a whole piece is still hanging in the balance. } 16... axb3 17. Qxb3 e5 18. Qb4 Qc7 { By the time the dust settles you are simply a knight behind, with the queen having escaped clean away. }) 16... Qb5 { Her queen finds the one square left open to her, all the way out on b five — but even that lonely square is being watched. } 17. Bxb5 { [%tail] Her last square was watched all along, so the bishop takes the queen for free right now. [%cal Gd3b5] } (17. Bd6 { A fancy-looking bishop move elsewhere ignores the simple truth that the queen was standing there, completely undefended. } 17... exd6 18. Bxb5 cxb5 19. Rc1 Rfe8 { The bishop you sent to d six simply gets traded away for nothing, while the queen escapes untouched. }) (17. Bc7 { Chasing after the rook with the bishop instead lets her queen slip free through the gap you have just left open. } 17... Qb7 18. Bxd8 Rxd8 19. f4 Qc7 { You end up winning only a rook here, when the whole queen was sitting there waiting to be taken instead. }) 17... cxb5 18. f3 { You tuck in a quiet pawn move — there is nothing left to calculate. A queen for a bishop, and the game is not remotely close. } 1-0
